hey what's up my name's samuel leeds i'm  a property investor i've been investing  in property for over a decade  and in this video i'm gonna be revealing  the worst property i ever  bought this is probably hands down the  worst house  it is so so bad i decided to do a video  about it now many people say to me  samuel why do you only talk about the  good side to property investing you're  talking about how to make money and how  things go well and i'm thinking to be  honest it's because  firstly i want you to succeed and  secondly  most of my properties are good and  there's very few properties that i've  bought and i've regretted buying  so i'm not going to paint a particularly  bad image i'm  just going to focus on what is the truth  however i do  think that you can learn more from bad  properties and bad experiences than good  sometimes  so if you're gonna hit the rocks and buy  a rubbish house at least be a lighthouse  to others which is what i'm being to you  right now so if you enjoy my channel  please  do smash the like button i want to see  the blue  thumb up so smash the like button also  if you're not subscribed to my channel  please do subscribe and turn the  notification bell on so you do not miss  an awesome video where you can learn  about property the worst house  i ever bought was in 2012 and  it was on durham road in durham now the  reason i bought this house was because  it was a no money down deal i  strategically creatively financed this  deal  in a joint venture partnership and my  brother holds it in his name  and i bought it for 104 000 pounds  however  the house sucks on every level it's a  little bit of an old house it looks kind  of nice and i thought this looks nice  it's no money down what could possibly  go wrong  but because it's in a bit of an old  house i've had continual problems with  things like damp  i've had the the roofs need fixing i've  spent  probably about 15 000 pounds in the last  eight years or so since i've owned it on  that property  and on top of that the house is worth  today  exactly what it was worth when i bought  it back in 2012.  so capital appreciation on it has been  pants the  maintenance on it have been terrible but  on top of that to make it  much much worse the tenants have been  terrible  that house seems to attract awful  tenants  now not the kind of awful tenants you  might think it's in a reasonably nice  area  you know it's not even nice everybody  it's not in a you know trash area with  bums and stuff  and i i've always spoke to the tenants  they've seemed lovely but they've just  never paid rent they're moving their pay  rent for a year and then they stop  paying rent and i'm like what the heck  then i have to evict them and they make  it difficult as possible it takes six  months to a victim and then finally i'm  like  ah it's over and then i move somebody  else in and the same thing happens again  so i did a calculation on on spreadsheet  on that particular property  and over the last eight and a half years  or however long it's been since i've  owned it guess how much profit i've made  on that property i have made  nothing no money in fact i've  if you add it all up with the money that  i've spent on it and the money that i've  made i'm actually down  financially right now and this is what  inspired me and prompted me to do the  video  that property is empty and i was like oh  do i even want to get another tenant  because the only thing worse than no  tenant is a bad tenant  and don't get me wrong by the way i know  i'm focusing on the bad right now  some people might say in the comments oh  just get a management company or oh why  don't you just do this or just  i've done all those things there's  always a very small  element of risk when you're buying a  property there's always a chance that a  tenant will come and they'll have  perfect references perfect credit and  then  they'll work they won't pay rent it is  possible it's unlikely but for some  reason this property just seems to have  the kiss of death on it it's empty right  now  and my wife went around to visit the  property and guess what  the old tenant has trashed the property  it is  filthy and we're gonna have to spend a  few thousand pounds getting it up to  scratch  to move a tenant back into the property  which is gonna at best make us 150 pound  a month profit  which is going to take probably about  two years to pay for the refurb of the  last tenant that trashed the house do  you know what you call that you call it  a  terrible investment so i'm really upset  about this house  i thought i'd share it with you what are  the lessons from this there's a few  lessons firstly is  just because a house is a free house  doesn't mean it's a good house it's got  to make you money it's got a cash flow  positive  at the time i was only like 20 years old  so i was growing my portfolio i was  taking on any houses that i could  now i'm more picky now i'd rather put in  10 grand  and have a good house the cash flow is  positive then put nothing in at all but  have a house it's actually potentially  going to lose me money so i think that's  the first lesson  next thing this is really important  every time you buy a property  yes there's a risk but what's going to  happen is you to have some properties  that perform  and what i mean by that is they're going  to perform as expected so if you expect  to put a tenant in  and they'll pay this and you expect the  return on investment to be say 15  percent  it's just going to perform nicely as  expected  you have some properties that  underperform  now those properties maybe there might  be a property that's prone to  maintenance or you might have to be a  bit unlucky with it but it's going to be  an underperforming property  and then you can have some properties  that over-perform and  they're going to shoot up in value and  you're going to have really good tenants  and you're going to put the rent up and  it's just going to be amazing  and you're going to make more money than  you thought now this is a really  important lesson firstly  expect that just be prepared that you're  going to have under performance  over performance and just performers  that's your portfolio it's gonna happen  now it's really important that you do  don't look at this as an overall  portfolio though now you might think  what are you talking about surely you  just need to look at the  whole portfolio as a whole yes you do  but you  also need to look at each individual  property what do i mean by this  every month i have a financial report of  all of my businesses all of my  properties and i want to see  how much have we turned over what were  our overheads what were our direct costs  and what were our  profit and what was our net profit  percentage those are the figures that i  want to know  every single month on my financial  report now my property business  i want a financial report of the whole  portfolio  and i want a financial report of every  single  individual house you need this let me  give you an example  of one of my students so one of my  students said to me samuel i've got  on when is wednesday by the way said  i've got three rent to serviced  accommodations and it's making  me 3 000 pounds a month i'm like  fantastic that's great  and you you might assume okay so a  thousand pound each i said  so you're making three thousand pound a  month off of the three houses how much  is each property making you  i'm not really sure i said well you need  to find that out  i told them about how to do your  financial reports and the figures you  need to run down  and this this student was actually a  student online academy and they went and  they and they did the financial report  and they came back to me they said  samuel guess what i said what's that  they said i'm making three thousand  pound a month from these three  properties but  one of them is making me one thousand  pound a month the other one  is making two thousand pound a month and  the third one is making me  nothing so in their mind they've got  three properties they're making three  thousand pound a month  great nice portfolio but actually  there's a weak  link in their portfolio which needs to  be cut needs to be chopped  and unless you do individual accounting  on in  each property that you have you won't  know where these weak links are  so my advice to you if you're a property  investor is make sure you know your  numbers have spreadsheets  every single month look at what your  whole portfolio  has made and what the net profit is and  the net profit percentage  but then also look at each individual  property and if you've got any weak  links  either sort them out fix the problem or  sell the property  and then or or get rid of it if it's a  rent to rent and then find another one  which is more like one of your high  performing  properties you're always going to have  low performing properties but you want  to have as few of them  as possible i hope you found this video  useful if you've got property investment  questions  let me know below i'd love to hear your  comments your feedback your thoughts and  if you enjoyed the video as i said  before  smash the like button subscribe to the  channel and turn on the notification  bell if you want to see more videos like  this you can watch a whole bunch more  here  and if you want to hear stories of  students that become successful in  property  you can do that right here and of course  you can subscribe right over here do  that now and i'll see you on the next  [Music]  video

